{title: Ride On, Ride On in Majesty}
{artist: Henry H. Milman / Winchester New (1690)}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Opening}
{key: C}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{score: ride-on-ride-on-in-majesty.abc}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Open Hymnal score (Ride_On_Ride_On_In_Majesty-Winchester_New)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Ride on! ride [F]on [Am]in [G7]majes[C]ty!
[C]Hark! [F]all [C]the [G]tribes [Em]Ho[Am]san[D]na [G]cry!
[G]O [C]Savior meek, pur[Dm]sue [C]Thy [G]road,
[C]With palms [F]and [G]scattered [Dm]gar[G7]ments [C]strowed.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Ride on! ride [F]on [Am]in [G7]majes[C]ty!
[C]In [F]low[C]ly [G]pomp [Em]ride [Am]on [D]to [G]die!
[G]O [C]Christ! Thy triumph [Dm]now [C]be[G]gin
[C]Over cap[F]tive [G]death and [Dm]con[G7]quered [C]sin.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]Ride on! Ride [F]on [Am]in [G7]majes[C]ty!
[C]The [F]an[C]gel [G]ar[Em]mies [Am]of [D]the [G]sky
[G]Look [C]down with sad and [Dm]won[C]d'ring [G]eyes
[C]Too see [F]th'ap[G]roaching [Dm]sac[G7]ri[C]fice.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C]Ride on! ride [F]on [Am]in [G7]majes[C]ty!
[C]Thy [F]last [C]and [G]fier[Em]cest [Am]strife [D]is [G]nigh;
[G]The [C]Father on His [Dm]sap[C]phire [G]throne,
[C]Expects [F]His [G]own a[Dm]noin[G7]ted [C]Son!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[C]Ride on! ride [F]on [Am]in [G7]majes[C]ty!
[C]In [F]low[C]ly [G]pomp [Em]ride [Am]on [D]to [G]die;
[G]Bow [C]Thy meek head to [Dm]mor[C]tal [G]pain!
[C]Then take, [F]oh [G]God! Thy [Dm]power, [G7]and [C]reign!
{end_of_verse}
